              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "paper · January 2026"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "OpenCivics Labs"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 3
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Bioregional Coordination: A Hybrid Framework for Network Commons",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://opencivics.co/labs/bioregioning",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "A long-form working paper laying out the two-body model behind SPIRIT's design: a small nonprofit that handles the legal and financial work, paired with a larger community body that holds the actual decision-making. Includes Elinor Ostrom's principles for shared resource management and a practical plan for how to build something like this."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "↗ Read external",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://opencivics.co/labs/bioregioning",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "blk_59k2sntw6a",
          "type": "text",
          "v": 1,
          "column": 1,
          "fields": {
            "content": {
              "type": "doc",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "essay · November 2025"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "omniharmonic"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "heading",
                  "attrs": {
                    "level": 4
                  },
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Collapse, Parallel Societies, and the Bioregional Imperative",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://omniharmonic.substack.com",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "On the slow unraveling of public institutions and why community-led, place-based networks — building real alternatives alongside the systems we still depend on — offer a third path between individual retreat and ideological exit."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "↗ Read external",
                      "marks": [
                        {
                          "type": "link",
                          "attrs": {
                            "href": "https://omniharmonic.substack.com",
                            "newTab": true
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
